  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Universal Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights in the Indo Pacific (TUSIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the work of the COVID-19 Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) Surge Initiative (C-Surge) in 2021-2024, TUSIP will continue high impact work that accelerates progress towards universal access to SRHR.  As a pillar of the Partnerships for a Healthy Region, its primary focus will be in six countries in Southeast Asia - Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar,  Philippines, Timor Leste and Vietnam. Elements of programming will also be delivered assisting Indonesia, Malaysia, Maldives and Nepal</narrative>
  </description>
